ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 33481, May 23, 2023>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on June 5, 2023.
Article 2 (Transitional measures concerning certificate of distinguished service to the State)
A certificate of distinguished service to the State or certificate of bereaved family member of a person of distinguished service to the State (including a certificate of distinguished service to independence or certificate of bereaved family member of a person of distinguished service to independence issued by applying the previous Article 101(1), pursuant to Article 42 of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service to Independence) issued pursuant to the previous Article 101(1) as at the time this Decree enters into force may be used until June 4, 2028.
Article 3 Omitted.
Article 4 (Relationship to other statutes or regulations)
Where, as at the time this Decree enters into force, any citation in any other statute or regulation (including statutes or regulations which are promulgated before the Enforcement of this Act but have not yet entered into force) of "certificate of distinguished service to the State", "certificate of bereaved family member of a person of distinguished service to the State", "certificate of distinguished service to independence", or "certificate of bereaved family member of a person of distinguished service to independence" is made, it shall be deemed to be a citation of a patriots and veterans registration card under this Decree.

